Q.What does this message mean? (man-in-the-middle attack)
WARNING: REMOTE HOST IDENTIFICATION HAS CHANGED!

It means:
"The server at 192.168.0.112 is presenting a different SSH identity than the one I previously trusted."
SSH blocks the connection until you verify the change.

fix:
ssh-keygen -f "/root/.ssh/known_hosts" -R "192.168.0.112"
This removes the old fingerprint.